  "result": "I found the bug and wrote a plan for the fix; nothing has been changed yet. I couldn't hand it to you through the normal plan-approval step because that tool isn't available in this session, so here it is.\n\n**The cause:** in `src/click/core.py:392`, a subcommand gets its parent's whole `default_map` instead of only its own section of it:\n\n```python\ndefault_map = parent.default_map\n```\n\nClick expects defaults for a subcommand to sit under that subcommand's name, like `default_map={\"sub\": {\"name\": \"x\"}}`. Because the subcommand gets the whole map, it looks for `\"name\"` at the top level, doesn't find it, and ignores the default.\n\n**The fix** is one line, so the subcommand picks out its own section:\n\n```python\ndefault_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)\n```\n\nIf there's no section for that subcommand, this gives `None`, which correctly means \"no defaults\".\n\n**Regression test:** I'll add `test_default_map_subcommand` to `tests/test_defaults.py`. It covers:\n- a group with one subcommand, using `{\"sub\": {\"name\": ...}}`\n- a group inside a group, using `{\"grp\": {\"leaf\": {\"x\": ...}}}`\n\n**To check it:** run `pytest tests/test_defaults.py -k subcommand`, which should fail before the fix and pass after it, then run the full `pytest tests` suite.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\defaults-configured-through-default-map-buzzing-twilight.md`. Tell me to go ahead and I'll make the change.",
